//==
// # Faceted shells: types (complexity sweep, chunk V9, TKT-377)
//
// The identification of a shell's poly-loop points and the implicit edge uses it implies, built
// once per shell (faceted.library.plato).

// The poly-loop points of one shell identified by coincidence, and the implicit edges they bound.
// PointRoots[k] is the class root (the smallest index of its class) of point k, the points taken
// bound by bound in ShellPolyBounds order; SortedUses is ImplicitEdgeUses over those bounds and
// roots, sorted ascending, so the uses of one implicit edge (key u / 2) are adjacent, the
// backward use (even) before the forward one (odd). A key is the rank of the edge's pair of
// point classes among the shell's distinct pairs in ascending order, below twice the use count
// at any point count (TKT-400; the packed key (a * N + b) * 2 overflowed a 32-bit Integer above
// about 32,768 points); EdgeLow[r] < EdgeHigh[r] are the two classes of the edge of rank r.
// Removes: CoincidenceRoots recomputed by each
// of ReducedCounts, ImplicitBoundaryCycleCount and ImplicitFreeEdgeKeys within one law, and the
// scan of every use per key in ImplicitFreeEdgeKeys and IsDefectiveImplicitEdge.
type ShellPolyEdges
    implements IValue
{
    PointRoots: Array<Integer>;
    SortedUses: Array<Integer>;
    EdgeLow: Array<Integer>;
    EdgeHigh: Array<Integer>;
}

// The implicit edge uses of some poly bounds, in use order, as three parallel arrays: use k runs
// between point classes Low[k] < High[k], and Forward[k] is 1 when the face runs it from Low to
// High (the bound's Orientation composed with the loop's order), 0 otherwise. A pair of
// consecutive points in one class is no edge and has no use.
type ImplicitEdgeUseList
    implements IValue
{
    Low: Array<Integer>;
    High: Array<Integer>;
    Forward: Array<Integer>;
}
